{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1547984-two-dumb-exigent-ideas","id":1547984,"title":"Two dumb exigent ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-27T15:49:10-08:00","id":1547984,"title":"Two dumb exigent ideas","content":"Like the title says, I have two ideas for Exigents:<br /> <br /> First - Chosen of Primordials - The chosen of Seventh Souless, the seventh god of Creation and the one who was supposed to the God of Primordials; the problem was what that meant exactly; originally the intermeditiary between the nascient gods and of the Primordials, although bit by bit that fell apart as the Incarnae were made and the Deva made more personal lines of communication to individual Primodial possible; When the Exalted began to rise up, Seventh Souless joined them as an advisor and double agent, and was rewarded with a nice job in the Bureau of Heaven after the War. But the whole position was a sinecure that occasionally involved talking to Gaia; after nearless endless years of pointless paper work, audits incase we has being bribed to give others access to Gaia and general derision, Seventh Souless asked the Unconquered Sun for some of the Fire of Exigence to do something useful with his power; his extreme sacrifice created 3 permenant exaltations that can last past the death of their chosen. Each of these 'Chosen of the Primordials' have slightly different powers in each incarnation but their main ability is to manifest three pseudo-deva called 'Peri', one for the Po soul, one of the Hun soul and one for the Exalted. Each Peri gives the Exalted specific charms that reflect their inner personality but also act as equal power servants. As a subset of this, each Peri can also create through summoning like rituals servitor races called Sub-Peri that serve their masters like 1st circle to 2nd and 3d circles. The Chosen of Primordials can also create Sub-Peri and give this ability to others (although all Sub-Peri are loyal to their chosen). All Chosen of the Primordials also have a relic inheritance from Seventh Souless - a Star Metal Artefact made from his falling star as he gave his essence up in the Flame of Exigence.<br /> <br /> Second - Chosen of the Lost Kingdom of K\u00f4r - K\u00f4r was a power and peaceful kingdom far removed from the Shogunate and maintaining First Age Marvels under a heredity line of Sorceror-Kings and their allies amongst gods banished from Yu-Shan in the shadow of the Usurpation for pro-solar and anti-sidereal opinions. However K\u00f4r was in the front line of a sizable Fair Folk invasion, and it's patron god, Mava-mava, barely managed to get the Fire of Exigence while the general of the Fair Folk breach the gates of K\u00f4r's capital; pouring all his power and some of the intruding Wyld's essence, he the crown Prince became one of the most powerful exalts ever, banishing the invasion with a mere hand ful of charms. However the prince then discovered the dreadful price that was paid; the entire kingdom of K\u00f4r was banished to Elsewhere and only feed by the endevoirs of the new Exalt. Chosen of the Lost Kingdom of K\u00f4r's powers are based on summoning things to and from K\u00f4r and to break down cultures to match K\u00f4r's. Occassionally people can enter or leave K\u00f4r by their own initiative (or more often dumb luck), with more people being accident sucked in to it that escaping it's twilight eternity. The Chosen of the Lost Kingdom of K\u00f4r must keep the kingdom thriving to maintain their own life and power, this means taking more resources, new blood and occaisionally heroes to deal with troubles all the while dumping waste, criminals and threats; but this bond also allows the citizens to sacrifice one of their number to extend the chosen's life; however each sacrifice alters the chosen a little - leading to some of it's scholars to wonder if the original Exalt has been totally replaced by another not once but multiple times (this could explain fluctuating power levels, forgotten memories, changes in personality, different appearances and swapping sex several times - if it's true.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T10:52:33-08:00","id":1548059,"title":"","content":"K\u00f4r sounds extremely similar to Beimeni-Ta from Adeimantus' write-up though the impression is that it's more his scale model now than an actual place with citizens.<br /> <br /> if you don't know who Adeimantus is,he'sbasically the coolest Raksha we've ever seen, who I'd describe as cosmic horror &quot;your world will look good on my mantlepiece&quot; Brainiac meets the King in Yellow because any knowledge about Beimeni-Ta allows him to manifest parts of it lesser societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-02T05:19:09-08:00","id":1548108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1547984-two-dumb-exigent-ideas?p=1548059#post1548059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">K\u00f4r sounds extremely similar to Beimeni-Ta from Adeimantus' write-up though the impression is that it's more his scale model now than an actual place with citizens.<br /> <br /> if you don't know who Adeimantus is,he'sbasically the coolest Raksha we've ever seen, who I'd describe as cosmic horror &quot;your world will look good on my mantlepiece&quot; Brainiac meets the King in Yellow because any knowledge about Beimeni-Ta allows him to manifest parts of it lesser societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, the Lost Kingdom of K\u00f4r's concept seems to fit what Beimeni-Ta's narrative to a tee, i was thinking of the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/247451/Adversaries-of-the-Righteous-Adeimantus\" target=\"_blank\">link </a>and all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now speaking of the God of Primordials thing..... No, just no.<br /> <br /> That patron is something that simply doesn't work with the lore, afaik. The Primordials are something from beyond creation, so not really valid as a concept for a deity's purview, god of fae or the Underworld might be more valid from that perspective - and even if it were <i>hypothetically</i> possible, someone having stewardship/oversight <i>over the Primordials</i>? Nope, would be erased before it could even exist.<br /> <br /> The idea of a intermediary between the nascent gods and of the Primordials.... that doesn't exactly roll great either, imho. If you are a middleperson between the gods and the titans, you probably are no god per se, more probably a deva or something else closer to the Primordials themselves.<br /> <br /> Supposing <i>such a role was needed in the first place</i>, because between access to sorcery, each Primordial having something like a score of Devas or more, who each have 7 souls of their own, i dare say &quot;more personal lines of communication to individual Primodials&quot; already existed before there was a Creation to be inhabited by mortal beings and given gods to manage its workings.<br /> <br /> Beside this, the &quot;UCS, please give me an exigence so i can make myself useful&quot; angle - that utterly ignores the fact an <i>Essence 5+ spirit can do a crapload of stuff </i>in and for Creation on its own simply by <b><i>acting in the first place</i></b> - can feel kind of very misguided, if you don't mind me saying.<br /> <br /> <br /> So i'd say that the idea of Seventh Souless as a divine patron for an exigent is broken and flawed on many levels. <i>If taken at face value and as truth</i>, that is.<br /> <br /> The Dark Mother for Liminals, Ketu for the Dream-Souled and the Voice In the Trench for the Spoken are there as example of elusive patrons on the Incarna or near-Incarna tier that are just as mysterious for their chosen as everybody else, if not more so. Seventh Souless could perfectly fit on such a niche, the idea of it as god of primordials either misunderstading, error or outright obfuscation/propaganda on the part of some of the few people in Creation or outside it that have even heard of the entity.<br /> <br /> Also, feel free to correct me if i got things utterly wrong, but aren't the mention and possible link to Primordials there as excuse/springboard for Devil-Tiger-esque multi-tiered soul shenanigans with the Peri and servitor-making in the form of the sub-Peri? If so, &quot;Seventh Souless&quot; being not really a god but some sort of elusive spirit of great might but not quite clear origins and nature might make for a better fit, imho.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the name &quot;Seventh Souless&quot; on itself makes me think it could be some sort of 3rd circle Deva/Demon that lost its components and yet managed to survive in some form, now making these chosen of its own as part of some abstruse gamble to somehow fill the emptiness left in its place with change. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> Just some ramblings and thoughts. Hope i didn't come out as too salty or anything like. See ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-31-2026, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T15:01:22-08:00","id":1548157,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was actual thinking that I might do something more with the Peri idea; the original idea was just a weird idea for an Exigent but something more substansive, not quite going Devil-Tiger, only limiting to two Peri and having abilities related to that. Not fully sure where else to go with that, but could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-03T20:21:44-08:00","id":1548174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1547984-two-dumb-exigent-ideas?p=1548157#post1548157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was actual thinking that I might do something more with the Peri idea; the original idea was just a weird idea for an Exigent but something more substansive, not quite going Devil-Tiger, only limiting to two Peri and having abilities related to that. Not fully sure where else to go with that, but could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters, does the idea of the Peri requires a sort of exalt? Considering it's connection to the dual souls of human beings in Creation it could just as well relate to Sorcery, thaumaturgy and all sorts of occult explorations or phenomena.<br /> <br /> That said, delving on the subject of <b>empowered</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulpa\" target=\"_blank\">higher </a>and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_(psychology)\" target=\"_blank\">lower</a> souls can also easily into explorations of the unconscious, dreams, inner mindscapes and spiritual journeys into realms of the self and beyond not unlike some of the themes of Mage: the Awakening, imho. Maybe a little of KotE (or Wraith), where H'un &amp; P'o are kind of a big deal too?<br /> Some possible parallels with either the Unwoven Coadjutors of 2e Green Sun Princes or the Shadow of Umbrals do come to mind, too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Exalted can be somewhat peculiar in their definition and qualities, if beings like Liminals, Hearteaters (or the mysterious Spoken of the Niobraran) serve as any indicator of potential of edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-03-2025, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}